the target language is: prolog.

% The promissory note of L4's legal examples (smucclaw/l4-ide,
% jl4/examples/legal/promissory-note.l4, Apache 2.0), written by hand as the
% L4 translator will write it: the timeless reading of the design notes l4.md
% section 4.1. The note is read over a history of payments that has already
% happened, and says how the note stands at the end of that history.
%
% L4 runs the note as a chain of obligations. While money is owed, the
% borrower must pay the next instalment within a number of days of the moment
% the obligation started. Paying it starts the same obligation again for what
% is still owed. Missing it starts a penalty obligation (the instalment plus 5
% per cent); missing that starts an obligation to pay everything owed, which
% has no deadline.
%
% How L4 notices a missed deadline (checked against L4's evaluator): only when
% the next payment arrives, or when the history says time has passed ("the
% clock reaches" below). That later event starts the next obligation, and is
% not itself counted as a payment of it.
%
% Money is in United States dollars throughout; L4's check of the currency is
% left out.

the templates are:
    the borrower pays *an amount* on *a date*; undefined.
    the clock reaches *a date*; undefined.
    something happens on *a date*.
    an obligation can start on *a date*.
    *a base* to the power of *a number* is *a value*.
    the monthly interest rate is *a rate*.
    the monthly instalment is *an amount*; memorable.
    the total repayment is *an amount*; memorable.
    the instalment due on a debt of *an amount* is *a due amount*.
    the instalments covered by a debt of *an amount* are *a number*.
    the instalment obligation on a debt of *an amount* starts on *a date*; memorable.
    the instalment obligation on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* has deadline *a deadline*; memorable.
    a payment of *an amount* on *a date* meets the instalment obligation on a debt of *a debt* started on *a start*.
    the instalment obligation on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* ends on *a day* with a payment of *a payment*; memorable.
    the instalment obligation on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* is missed on *a day*; memorable.
    the penalty obligation on a debt of *an amount* starts on *a date*; memorable.
    the penalty obligation on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* has deadline *a deadline*; memorable.
    a payment of *an amount* on *a date* meets the penalty obligation on a debt of *a debt* started on *a start*.
    the penalty obligation on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* ends on *a day* with a payment.
    the penalty obligation on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* is missed on *a day*.
    the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of *an amount* starts on *a date*.
    all the debts on a debt of *an amount* are *a total*.
    the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of *an amount* started on *a date* ends on *a day*.
    the note is fulfilled on *a date*.
    the note is pending with *an obligation* on a debt of *an amount* since *a date*.

the knowledge base promissory note includes:

% The loan's terms (L4: Basic Definitions and Repayment Terms).

the monthly interest rate is a rate if
    the rate = 0.15 / 12.

a base to the power of a number is a value if
    the number = 0
    and the value = 1.

a base to the power of a number is a value if
    the number > 0
    and a smaller number = the number - 1
    and the base to the power of the smaller number is a smaller value
    and the value = the base * the smaller value.

the monthly instalment is an amount if
    the monthly interest rate is a rate
    and a base = 1 + the rate
    and the base to the power of 12 is a factor
    and the amount = 25000 * (the rate * the factor) / (the factor - 1).

the total repayment is an amount if
    the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the amount = the instalment * 12.

% What is due on a debt: the monthly instalment, or what is left if that is less.

the instalment due on a debt of an amount is a due amount if
    the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the minimum of the instalment and the amount is the due amount.

the instalments covered by a debt of an amount are a number if
    the total repayment is a total
    and the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the number = (the total - the amount) / the instalment.

something happens on a date if
    the borrower pays an amount on the date.

something happens on a date if
    the clock reaches the date.

an obligation can start on 2025-02-04.

an obligation can start on a date if
    something happens on the date.

% The instalment obligation (L4: Payment Obligations).

the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount starts on 2025-02-04 if
    the total repayment is the amount.

the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount starts on a date if
    the borrower pays a payment on the date
    and the instalment obligation on a debt of an earlier amount started on an earlier date ends on the date with a payment of a payment
    and the amount = the earlier amount - the payment
    and the amount > 0.

% L4 counts the deadline from the day the obligation started, and adds the
% grace period of 10 days.
the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date has deadline a deadline if
    the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount starts on the date
    and the instalments covered by a debt of the amount are a number
    and a count = ceiling((the number + 1) * 30.436875) + 10
    and the deadline is the count days after the date.

a payment of an amount on a date meets the instalment obligation on a debt of a debt started on a start if
    the borrower pays the amount on the date
    and an obligation can start on the start
    and the date is after the start
    and the instalment obligation on a debt of the debt started on the start has deadline a deadline
    and the date is before or equal to the deadline
    and the instalment due on a debt of the debt is a due amount
    and the amount >= the due amount - 0.05.

% The first event that decides the obligation: a payment that meets it, or
% anything that happens after its deadline.
the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date ends on a day with a payment of a payment if
    a payment of the payment on the day meets the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date
    and it is not the case that
        something happens on an earlier day
        and the earlier day is after the date
        and the earlier day is before the day
        and the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date has deadline a deadline
        and the earlier day is after the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        a payment of an other payment on an other day meets the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date
        and the other day is before the day.

the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date is missed on a day if
    something happens on the day
    and an obligation can start on the date
    and the date is before the day
    and the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date has deadline a deadline
    and the day is after the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date ends on a paid day with a payment of a payment
    and it is not the case that
        something happens on an earlier day
        and the earlier day is after the deadline
        and the earlier day is before the day.

% The penalty obligation (L4: the first LEST).

the penalty obligation on a debt of an amount starts on a date if
    something happens on the date
    and an obligation can start on a start
    and the start is before the date
    and the instalment obligation on a debt of the amount started on a start is missed on the date.

the penalty obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date has deadline a deadline if
    the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount starts on the date
    and the instalments covered by a debt of the amount are a number
    and a count = ceiling((the number + 1) * 30.436875) + 30
    and the deadline is the count days after the date.

a payment of an amount on a date meets the penalty obligation on a debt of a debt started on a start if
    the borrower pays the amount on the date
    and an obligation can start on the start
    and the date is after the start
    and the penalty obligation on a debt of the debt started on the start has deadline a deadline
    and the date is before or equal to the deadline
    and the instalment due on a debt of the debt is a due amount
    and the amount >= the due amount * 1.05 - 0.05.

the penalty obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date ends on a day with a payment if
    a payment of a payment on the day meets the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date
    and it is not the case that
        something happens on an earlier day
        and the earlier day is after the date
        and the earlier day is before the day
        and the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date has deadline a deadline
        and the earlier day is after the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        a payment of an other payment on an other day meets the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date
        and the other day is before the day.

the penalty obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date is missed on a day if
    something happens on the day
    and an obligation can start on the date
    and the date is before the day
    and the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date has deadline a deadline
    and the day is after the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount started on the date ends on a paid day with a payment
    and it is not the case that
        something happens on an earlier day
        and the earlier day is after the deadline
        and the earlier day is before the day.

% The obligation to pay all debts (L4: the second LEST). It has no deadline.

the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of an amount starts on a date if
    something happens on the date
    and an obligation can start on a start
    and the start is before the date
    and the penalty obligation on a debt of the amount started on a start is missed on the date.

all the debts on a debt of an amount are a total if
    the instalment due on a debt of the amount is a due amount
    and the total = the amount + the due amount * 0.05.

the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of an amount started on a date ends on a day if
    the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of the amount starts on the date
    and all the debts on a debt of the amount are a total
    and the borrower pays a payment on the day
    and the day is after the date
    and the payment >= the total - 0.05
    and it is not the case that
        the borrower pays an other payment on an other day
        and the other day is after the date
        and the other day is before the day
        and the other payment >= the total - 0.05.

% How the note stands.

the note is fulfilled on a day if
    the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date ends on the day with a payment of a payment
    and the amount - the payment <= 0.

the note is fulfilled on a day if
    the penalty obligation on a debt of an amount started on a date ends on the day with a payment.

the note is fulfilled on a day if
    the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of an amount started on a date ends on the day.

the note is pending with the instalment obligation on a debt of an amount since a date if
    the instalment obligation on a debt of a debt starts on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the instalment obligation on a debt of the debt started on the date ends on a day with a payment of a payment
    and it is not the case that
        the instalment obligation on a debt of the debt started on the date is missed on a day
    and the amount = round(the debt * 100) / 100.

the note is pending with the penalty obligation on a debt of an amount since a date if
    the penalty obligation on a debt of a debt starts on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the penalty obligation on a debt of the debt started on the date ends on a day with a payment
    and it is not the case that
        the penalty obligation on a debt of the debt started on the date is missed on a day
    and the amount = round(the debt * 100) / 100.

the note is pending with the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of an amount since a date if
    the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of a debt starts on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the obligation to pay all debts on a debt of the debt started on the date ends on a day
    and the amount = round(the debt * 100) / 100.

query fulfilled is:
    the note is fulfilled on which date.

query pending is:
    the note is pending with which obligation on a debt of which amount since which date.

query instalment is:
    the monthly instalment is which amount.

